# Nothing here is needed for `npm run dev`: the AI key is typed into the app and stays in this
# browser (BYOK), and the dev proxy accepts any local target.
#
# Production only. Cloudflare Pages reads this as an environment variable, set under
# Settings > Environment variables, or locally via `npx wrangler pages dev dist` picking up `.env`.
#
# AI_PROXY_ALLOWED_HOSTS adds hosts to the /api/ai-proxy relay allowlist, comma or space separated,
# merged over the built-in defaults: api.openai.com, api.anthropic.com,
# generativelanguage.googleapis.com, dashscope.aliyuncs.com, dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com,
# token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com.
# Names are matched exactly - a suffix match would accept api.openai.com.attacker.test - and
# private/loopback targets stay blocked at the edge whatever is listed here.
#
# Wrangler reads this for `npm run pages:local`. Prefer .dev.vars instead? Use one or the other:
# when a .dev.vars file exists, wrangler ignores .env files entirely.
#
# AI_PROXY_ALLOWED_HOSTS=gateway.example.com, llm.internal.example

# --- Admin stats (all optional; see README > Admin stats) ---
# Random secret for the daily-rotating IP hash. Without it no IP hash is stored at all.
# Set as an encrypted variable in Pages, never commit a real value.
# ANALYTICS_SALT=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
#
# Cloudflare Access (Zero Trust) values. The stats API refuses every request unless BOTH are set
# and the Access JWT verifies, so a misconfigured Access policy fails closed.
# ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=yourteam.cloudflareaccess.com
# ACCESS_AUD=<Application Audience (AUD) tag from the Access application>
#
# Local only (wrangler pages dev): skip the JWT check, honoured on localhost/127.0.0.1 exclusively.
# STATS_DEV_BYPASS=1
